  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Calculate the minor of the entry ${x}_{21}$ in the matrix\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 11-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-33-0 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
